  "rules": [
    "Every peak figure is DENSE. When a vendor quotes a sparse figure, the dense value is stored with quoted_sparse, and value must equal quoted_sparse / 2.",
    "Every figure names a source key from sources and a confidence (high, med, low). Only high or med measured data may be used to calibrate; low data is cross-check only.",
    "Per-GPU MLPerf throughput is never stored; it is computed as system_result / accelerators, because MLPerf reports systems.",
    "SKU power bins are not mixed: calibration uses the HGX/DGX bins, because the MLPerf calibration systems are DGX systems.",
    "Source conflicts are kept, with the alternatives and the resolution, never silently resolved.",
    "Changing a tolerance, the calibration set, or the held-out set after C1 starts is an evaluator change and needs the owner's approval (plan section 4, item 4)."
  ],
